
------------------------------
## Flask & MongoDB User Auth Logging App
A lightweight Flask web application that accepts user credentials via a form, securely saves them into a MongoDB database, and provides a protected workflow using the POST-Redirect-GET pattern.
## 🚀 Features

* User Login Form: Collects names and passwords via a dynamic interface.
* Database Logging: Real-time data storage in MongoDB.
* Smart Redirects: Fixes form resubmission bugs by redirecting to a clean /success-page.
* Data Viewer: A JSON API endpoint (/view) to inspect all records currently inside the database collection.

------------------------------
## 🛠️ Prerequisites
Before running this application, make sure you have installed:

* Python 3.8+
* MongoDB (Atlas cloud cluster or a local instance)

------------------------------
## 📥 Getting Started## 1. Clone or set up your directory
Create a project folder and drop your app.py script inside it along with your web layout:

your-project-folder/
├── templates/
│   └── index.html
├── .env
├── app.py
└── README.md

## 2. Install dependencies
Run the following command in your terminal to install the required packages:

pip install flask pymongo python-dotenv

## 3. Configure Environment Variables
Create a file named .env in the root directory of your project. Add your MongoDB connection string to it:

URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster0.mongodb.net/myDatabase?retryWrites=true&w=majority

⚠️ Make sure to replace <username>, <password>, and the cluster URL with your actual MongoDB credentials.

------------------------------
## 💻 Running the App
Start the Flask development server by executing:

python app.py

The application will spin up in debug mode and become accessible at http://127.0.0.1:5000.
------------------------------
## 🔌 API Endpoints Reference

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| /login | GET | Renders the login page template (index.html). |
| /login | POST | Validates parameters, saves them to MongoDB, and redirects. |
| /success-page | GET | Displays a JSON confirmation of a successful submission. |
| /view | GET | Fetches and returns all database entries safely serialized as JSON. |

------------------------------


